[expr.prim.fold]/2: folds over a one-element pack reduce to the single pattern
instance (binary folds to one application against the init operand); previously
the one-element case skipped the fold rewrite and the residual node degraded to
`true`.  Covers unary right/left, binary, comma and && shapes at one and more
elements.  Runtime-verified against g++ and clang++.
